[s0l0!-header][h1]New Line[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

The [b]cout [/b]object does not insert a line break at the end of the output. 
One way to print two lines is to use the [b]endl [/b]manipulator, which will put in a line break. [code format="cpp" codeId="172"]#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main()
{
  cout << "Hello world!" << [b]endl[/b];
  cout << "I love programming!";
  return 0;
}[/code]
[note]Run the code and see how it works![/note]

